crypto-ffi: encrypted attachments of Otaku (otaku.5)

Additions only, against tag matrix-sdk-crypto-0.19.1 (commit
b18166c68bb958a21f0bca8b2d8320cb53583362), after 0001 to 0005. No behaviour
of an existing call changes. Otaku D-381, ADR-0029 §10 (photos and voice
messages encrypted on the device, MSG-41 to MSG-43).

src/attachments.rs: two free functions, without an Olm machine nor a store,
the counterparts of Attachment.encrypt / Attachment.decrypt of
matrix-sdk-crypto-wasm, over the same types of matrix-sdk-crypto:
- attachment_encrypt(data) -> EncryptedAttachment { encrypted_data,
  media_encryption_info }: AttachmentEncryptor (fresh random key and IV of
  the library, AES-256-CTR, SHA-256 of the ciphertext), then the JSON of
  MediaEncryptionInfo (serde of the library: v, key, iv, hashes).
- attachment_decrypt(encrypted_data, media_encryption_info) -> clear:
  MediaEncryptionInfo read by serde, AttachmentDecryptor (EncryptedFile v2
  only, SHA-256 of the data checked at its end), no output otherwise.
Sizes: 1 byte to 25 MiB (CHAT_MEDIA_CEILING_BYTES of Otaku); info at most
4 096 bytes. Outputs reserved with try_reserve_exact (insufficient_memory
instead of an abort). Fixed error codes (AttachmentError): attachment_input,
attachment_info, attachment_corrupted, insufficient_memory, internal. The
clear input, the info text and a clear refused by the hash are erased on
return (Zeroizing).

No new dependency, Cargo.toml and Cargo.lock unchanged: matrix-sdk-crypto
(AttachmentEncryptor, AttachmentDecryptor, MediaEncryptionInfo, already
compiled into the library), serde_json, thiserror, zeroize, and, for the
tests only, sha2 and vodozemac (base64), all already dependencies of
matrix-sdk-crypto-ffi.

Tests (cargo test -p matrix-sdk-crypto-ffi --lib attachments): the common
vectors of Otaku (fixtures/otaku/attachment-v2.json, computed by node:crypto,
same bytes as the Otaku repository, checked by SHA-256; among them the
example of matrix-sdk-crypto's own tests and a counter that carries past
2^64), an altered, truncated or longer ciphertext, the round trip and the
shape of the info, the bounds, infos refused (v1, other versions,
no hash, key or IV of the wrong size, not JSON, too long), and the
exported surface.

Not compiled locally (no Rust toolchain on the workstation): the checks
job of the workflow is the first compilation.

